<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baldwin I of Flanders</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 879</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Baldwin Iron Arm</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baldwin I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, called Iron Arm, was the first count of Flanders. In 862 he eloped with Judith, daughter of the West Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a>, who after reconciliation gave him lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruges">Bruges</a> to defend against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> raids. His march became the County of Flanders, and his descendants ruled it for over two centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-of-flanders.jpg" alt="Baldwin I of Flanders" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zeisterre · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boudewyn_I_van_Vlaanderen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
